# GPForum's hourly jobs and daily partition window on FreeBSD: the
# counterpart of deploy/systemd's two timers and of the launchd jobs.
# cron(8) reads this file from /usr/local/etc/cron.d/, in the system
# crontab's format, whose sixth field is the account each command runs as.
# `gpforum service print rc` writes it with this host's paths.
#
# bin/gpforum reads the service's environment file itself, as the rc scripts
# do, and finds the Perl and the dependencies this checkout installed; it is
# a Perl script, so PATH names /usr/local/bin, where the perl5 package puts
# perl and cron's own PATH does not look. cron mails what each run prints to
# the account. Give the daily run another minute on each node: the runs take
# an advisory lock, and one that does not get it does nothing.
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
#
# minute hour mday month wday who command
0 * * * * gpforum /usr/local/www/gpforum/bin/gpforum scheduled-jobs --once --limit 100
17 3 * * * gpforum /usr/local/www/gpforum/bin/gpforum partitions --apply
